-- title:
--   Definitions for Asymptotic state transformations of continuous variable resources
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *Asymptotic state transformations of continuous variable resources* (arXiv:2010.00044) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `BoundedSelfAdjoint`: PDF p.3: bounded self-adjoint operators on the entire Hilbert space.
--   - `weakPositiveTopology`: PDF pp.3–4: the weak topology on the positive trace-class cone, tested against all bounded self-adjoint operators, rather than just compact ones.
--   - `normPositiveTopology`: PDF p.4: restriction of the accepted nuclear trace-norm topology to the cone.
--   - `weakOperatorPositiveTopology`: PDF p.3: WOT on the self-adjoint positive cone is generated by all quadratic forms.
--   - `weakStateTopology`: PDF pp.3–4: weak topology restricted to trace-one positive states.
--   - `weakOperatorStateTopology`: PDF pp.3–4: WOT restricted to trace-one positive states.
--   - `measuredKLSummand`: PDF p.5: a single classical KL summand, extended on support failure. No trace-correction term is added for an unnormalized second argument.
--   - `FinitePOVM`: PDF pp.3,5: exactly finite-outcome POVMs of positive bounded effects.
--   - `traceClassMeasuredEntropyBits`: PDF p.5, (10), extended to the positive trace-class second argument of Lemma 20, p.11. EReal retains negative finite values when Tr sigma exceeds one. The input rho is always a positive trace-one state. The accepted Bridge50.P11 measuredEntropy is a natural-log variational program on algebra functionals, not this finite-POVM definition with an unnormalized trace-class reference. Source correction: printed (10), p.5, repeats P_rho in both arguments. Changed: the second distribution is P_sigma. Why: the surrounding two-state definition and the explicit Tr(sigma E_x) calculation on pp.19-20 require it; the literal printed expression would be identically zero on normalized rho.
--   - `StrictlyPositiveQuadraticForm`: PDF pp.11,18: strict positivity means a positive quadratic form on every nonzero vector, without a uniform spectral lower bound. The accepted Dependency50.P37.StrictlyPositive is instead a predicate on CP maps.
--   - `UniformlyPositive`: PDF p.18: L has some positive lower spectral bound depending on L. The proof explicitly uses L >= delta I. This is stronger than zero kernel.
--   - `twoPower`: PDF pp.11,18: the bounded positive exponential 2^h, via real continuous functional calculus on the bounded spectrum of a self-adjoint h.
--   - `logarithmicExpectation`: PDF pp.18–19: extended logarithmic expectation. The continuous bounded-below spectral cutoffs log2(max(x,1/(n+1))) decrease to log2(x). The infimum is in EReal, so nonintegrable negative logarithmic tails give minus infinity. Only positive L and trace-one rho are used; this is not cfc Real.log at zero.
--   - `exponentialProgram`: PDF p.11, (23)–(24): optimization over all bounded self-adjoint h. The Bool selects the linear penalty (true) or logarithmic penalty (false). The false branch is used only with sigma nonzero.
--   - `positiveProgram`: PDF p.11, (25)–(28): optimization over bounded uniformly positive L (uniform=true) or bounded strictly positive L (uniform=false), with either penalty. The logarithmic penalty is used only with sigma nonzero.
--   - `zeroPositive`: PDF p.20, Remark 32: the zero positive trace-class operator, explicitly without a normalization or nonzero requirement.
-- source:
--   Asymptotic state transformations of continuous variable resources, arXiv:2010.00044v3, https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.00044v3

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Dependency50_P13
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Dependency50_P39
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Information100_P62

/-!
Ferrari, Lami, Theurer and Plenio, arXiv:2010.00044v3.
Drafted subset: Corollary 3, Remark 4, Lemma 20, Remark 32.
All remaining planned nodes are explicitly deferred in HARD.md and GAPS.json.
The independent-paper override permits the inspected accepted-library imports.
Only definition bodies are reused. Compilation and independent review are pending.
